<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The adaptive icon's background layer. `tauri icon` writes this file as #fff,
  and the value is changed here by hand for the same reason the CAMERA
  permission in AndroidManifest.xml is: tauri.conf.json has no field that can
  express it, so the delta lives in this committed gen/ tree. Re-running
  `tauri icon` resets it to white, so check this file in the diff.

  a8462d is the accent token in src/web/tokens.js, which is where the colour
  actually lives. The foreground PNG is full bleed accent already, so this
  layer is only visible in the parallax a launcher applies when it shifts the
  two layers against each other; white there flashes a pale edge on an
  otherwise solid tile.

  Note that no two-hyphen sequence appears anywhere above. XML forbids it
  inside a comment, and this repo's prose style reaches for it as an em dash
  constantly. Android's manifest merger reports the result as a bare "Error
  parsing" with no line number, which is a slow thing to find twice, and this
  file is the second time.
-->
<resources>
  <color name="ic_launcher_background">#a8462d</color>
</resources>
